# Human-in-the-loop (write actions)

Adapted from ADOP’s discovery gate. Same principle, different domain: this agent diagnoses mock pipelines and may propose remediations.

## Read vs write

- Read tools may run without approval: `get_pipeline_metrics`, `search_logs`, `get_recent_deploys`, incident lookup.
- Write/remediation tools must pause for a human: `restart_consumer`, `scale_partitions`, `open_ticket`, and any future write action.

## Required behavior

- Propose the write action with the reason and expected effect.
- Stop and wait for approve or reject. Do not invent approval.
- On reject, do not run the action; record the decision.
- On approve, run the simulated action, then store the incident in memory.
- Keep secrets out of source. Use `.env` only.

## Do not copy from ADOP

Do not pull Bronze/Silver/Gold zone questions, Airflow/Glue/SQL rules, or ADOP discovery hooks into this repo. Those belong to the ADOP project only.
